  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tioguanine may be associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23) through a series of indirect pathways. Both Tioguanine and the target leukemia are linked to Glasdegib, which is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23), and also to Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin, another agent indicated for the same leukemia. This indicates that Tioguanine may share a common pathway of action with these agents, potentially through the same or related molecular mechanisms. The evidence is supported by high scores in multiple paths, suggesting a consistent relationship across different indications. However, the exact mechanism by which Tioguanine influences the disease remains unclear, and further research is needed to determine its role in the pathogenesis of this leukemia.",
